{
  "id": "29905_gitai",
  "headword": "{擬態|ぎたい}",
  "reading": "ぎたい",
  "romaji": "gitai",
  "part_of_speech": "noun",
  "gloss": "mimicry; camouflage",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "mimicry; camouflage (of an animal)",
      "explanation": "The way an animal resembles its surroundings or another creature — in color, shape, or pattern — to hide from predators or prey. Used as a suru-verb ({擬態|ぎたい}する) meaning to disguise oneself in this way."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29905_gitai_ex1",
      "japanese": "この{虫|むし}は{擬態|ぎたい}が{上手|じょうず}だ。",
      "english": "This insect is good at camouflage.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29905_gitai_ex2",
      "japanese": "カマキリは{葉|は}に{擬態|ぎたい}して{身|み}を{隠|かく}す。",
      "english": "The praying mantis camouflages itself as a leaf to hide.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29905_gitai_ex3",
      "japanese": "{昆虫|こんちゅう}の{擬態|ぎたい}は、{敵|てき}から{身|み}を{守|まも}るための{仕組|しく}みだ。",
      "english": "Insect mimicry is a mechanism for protecting themselves from enemies.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A biology term for the way an organism mimics its surroundings or another species for protection. Commonly used as a suru-verb: {擬態|ぎたい}する (to camouflage oneself, to mimic).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {葉|は}に{擬態|ぎたい}する: to camouflage as a leaf\n- {擬態|ぎたい}する{昆虫|こんちゅう}: an insect that uses mimicry\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {保護色|ほごしょく}: protective coloration — blending in by color alone, a narrower idea than {擬態|ぎたい}",
